      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); \"><img alt=\"\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/images/production/quesImages/qImage696799ccce9b94f4b9b4531b.png\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); \">Conclusions:</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); \"><span style=\"text-align: center;\">I. Some planets are moons → </span><span style=\"font-weight: bolder; text-align: center;\">Does not follow</span><span style=\"text-align: center;\"> (As there is no direct relation between planets and moons, so it is possible but not definitely true)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); \">II. All moons being stars is a possibility → <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">Follow</span> (As some stars are moons, so the possibility of all moons being stars exists as it does not contradict the given statements)</p>\n",
